​You need to specify show_guide = TRUE as an argument to geom_abline (it defaults to not showing guides, as you discovered).​

  Disclaimer:
​​

  I have posted the same question on stackoverflow (http://stackoverflow.com/questions/29988050/ggplot2-does-not-display-legends-for-features-within-geom-abline).
  Is this encouraged, discouraged, doesn't matter?

​I would say discouraged, because now that you have an answer here anyone answering the stack overflow question is wasting their time.

Best,
Ista​

library(ggplot2);

xy_data    = data.frame(x=runif(100, min=-0.5, max=0.5),
                        y=runif(100, min=-0.5, max=0.5));

slope_data = data.frame(slope  = c(-1, -0.5, 0.5, 1.0),
                        model  = paste0("m", seq(1,4)),
                        robust = rep(c("Robust", "Non-robust"), 2))

merged_data = merge(xy_data, slope_data)

slope_plot =
  ggplot()+
  geom_point(data=xy_data,     aes(x=x, y=y))+
  geom_abline(data=slope_data, aes(intercept=0, slope=slope, color=model, linetype=robust))

ggsave(plot=slope_plot, file="no_legend_slope_plot.png")

